{"id":"word:hebrew:H3966","type":"word","title":"מְאֹד","subtitle":"H3966 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, vehemence , i.e. (with or without preposition) vehemently ; by implication, wholly , speedily , etc. (often with other words as an intensive or superlative; especially when repeated)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מְאֹד (H3966) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 300 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מְאֹד (mᵉʼôd) means properly, vehemence , i.e. (with or without preposition) vehemently ; by implication, wholly , speedily , etc. (often with other words as an intensive or superlative; especially when repeated) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 10 4."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מְאֹד","transliteration":"mᵉʼôd","pronunciation":"meh-ode'","strong":"H3966","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3966","partOfSpeech":"a","forms":["מְאֹֽד","מְאֹ֑ד","מְאֹ֔ד","מְאֹ֖ד","מְאֹד֙"],"morphs":[["HD",291],["HR/D",6],["HR/Ncmsa",1],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",1],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, vehemence , i.e. (with or without preposition) vehemently ; by implication, wholly , speedily , etc. (often with other words as an intensive or superlative; especially when repeated)","usage":"diligently, especially, exceeding(-ly), far, fast, good, great(-ly), × louder and louder, might(-ily, -y), (so) much, quickly, (so) sore, utterly, very ( much, sore), well.","full":"H3966. meod מְאֹד noun masculine muchness, force, abundance, exceedingly (compare Assyrian mu'du , abundance , Hom ZMG 1878, 711 ('treasures ana mu'di, in abundance' ) Dl HWB 399 ): — 1 force, might , Deut 6:5 וּבְכָלמְֿאֹדֶ֑ךָ and with all thy might ; hence 2Kin 23:25 . 2 in different idioms (298 t.) to express the idea of exceedingly, greatly, very (whether of magnitude or degree): a. (so mostly) as adverb accusative, qualifying both adjectives and obs., Gen 1:31 מְאֹד טוֺב good exceedingly , 4:5 מְאֹד לְקַיִן וַיִּחַד and Cain was wroth exceedingly , 7:18 וַיִּגְבְּרוּ הַמַּיִם וַיִּרְבּוּ מְאֹד , 12:14 ; 13:2 וְאַבְרָם כָּבֵד מְאֹד בַּמִּקְנֶה , 13:13 לי ׳חַטָּאִים מאד , 18:20 ; 19:3 , 9 ; 21:11 ; 24:16 , 35 , + often, Psa 46:2 בְצָרוֺת עֶזְרָה מְאֹד נִמְצָא as a help in troubles, to be found (= present) exceedingly ; with an infinitive Isa 47:9 מְאֹד חֲבָרַיִח בְּעָצְמַת despite of thy spells being very numerous, Josh 9:13 מְאֹד הַדֶּרֶךְ מֵרֹב , 1Kin 7:47 ; מְאֹד הַרְבֵּה Gen 15:1 ; 41:49 ; Deut 3:5 +, for which in the later language is found מְאֹד לָרֹב Zech 14:14 ; 2Chr 4:18 ; 9:9 (in 1Kin 10:10 מְאֹד הַרְבֵּה ); 2Chr 24:24 ; 30:13 , and even מְאֹד לְהַרְבֵּה 11:12 ; 16:8 . מְאֹד is not usually separated from the word it qualifies by more than one or two words (as Gen 20:8 וייראו מאד האנשׁים , Num 11:10 י אף ׳ויחר מאד ); see, however, Deut 30:14 ; Judg 12:2 ; 2Sam 12:5 ; 1Kin 11:19 ; Psa 31:12 . It precedes its verb, Psalm 47:10 נַעֲלָה מְאֹד (hence 97:9 ), 92:6 . b. עַדמְֿאֹד up to abundance, to a great degree, exceedingly , Gen 27:33 ׳עַדמֿ גְּדֹלָה חֲדָדָה , 27:34 ; 1Sam 11:15 מ עד ֗֗֗ ׳וישׂמח , 25:36 עַדמֿ ׳שִׁכֹּר וְהוּא , 2Sam 2:17 ; 1Kin 1:4 ; Isa 64:8 (compare Lam 5:22 ), 5:11 ; Psa 38:7 ; 38:9 ; 119:8 ; 119:43 ; 119:51 ; 119:107 ; Dan 8:8 ; 11:25 . c. עַדלִֿמְאֹד (see לְ עַד ) 2Chr 16:14 . d. duplicated (Ges § 113k ), Gen 7:19 מ גָָּֽבְרוּ ׳וְהַמַּיִם ׳מ , 30:43 ; Num 14:7 ; 1Kin 7:47 ; 2Kin 10:4 ; Ezek 37:10 . e. מְאֹד בִּמְאֹד literally with muchness, muchness , Gen 17:2 , 6 , 20 ; Exod 1:7 (all P), Ezek 9:9 ; 16:13 .","rootNote":"from the same as 181 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 10 4","keyReferences":["1Chr 10 4","1Chr 16 25","1Chr 18 8","1Chr 19 5","1Chr 20 2","1Chr 21 8","1Chr 21 8","1Chr 21 13"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":300,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 10 4","boo